Third-party notices — myne-website
=================================

The shipped artefact is the static site in `dist/` (`pnpm build`), deployed to
`myne.md`. Three things about it are worth stating precisely, because the
obvious sentence ("the site bundles its dependencies") is false in both
directions: it would over-claim on the build tools and under-claim on the fonts.


No framework runtime ships
--------------------------

`client:*` appears nowhere under `src/`. Astro only emits its hydration runtime
for a component that asks for it, so the scripts the built site serves are the
ones this repository authors — there is no React/Vue/Svelte runtime, and no
Astro client runtime, in any page.

That is a fact about today and not a promise, so it is checked rather than
believed: `scripts/notice.test.mjs` fails if a `client:*` directive appears,
which is the same moment this file stops being complete.

Verify:

  grep -rn 'client:' src/


Bundled webfonts — SIL Open Font License 1.1
--------------------------------------------

  Inter            ·  The Inter Project Authors  (https://github.com/rsms/inter)
  JetBrains Mono   ·  The JetBrains Mono Project Authors  (https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono)

Both are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 and are served from this
origin rather than from a font CDN, which is a privacy decision and a licence one
at the same time: a `fonts.gstatic.com` request would leak every visitor's IP on
first paint. OFL-1.1 §2 requires the copyright notice and the licence to travel
with each copy, so they ship as:

  public/fonts/OFL.txt    →  /fonts/OFL.txt in the built site

It is the same file the application commits at `public/fonts/LICENSE.txt`, byte
for byte, so the two copies cannot drift apart.


Build-time only, not redistributed
----------------------------------

  astro, @astrojs/rss, @astrojs/sitemap, markdown-it
        Site generation. `markdown-it` renders the ledger RSS feed at build
        time; none of these reaches the browser.
  sharp, satori, @resvg/resvg-js, @fontsource/inter
        Open Graph image generation, at build time.
  @fontsource/jetbrains-mono
        A DEPENDENCY, not a devDependency, but what it contributes to the site
        is the JetBrains Mono font files, whose licence is the OFL text above.
        Its CSS is inlined by the bundler and is generated, not authored
        third-party code.
  @astrojs/check, @types/markdown-it, typescript
        Type-checking, at author time.


